From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: WayZer <himc.wicp@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 12 Sep 2026 23:24:39 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] FIX.C(Net) ignore unit spawn packets before world load

UnitSpawn packets are added to the world during handled(), so receiving
one while the world is still empty (during connect or after a reset)
crashes in PhysicsProcess.init -> World.getQuadBounds with
"World is empty".

Drop them on the client when world.height() == 0; the unit is synced
normally via snapshots after the world loads.
---
 core/src/mindustry/net/Net.java | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/core/src/mindustry/net/Net.java b/core/src/mindustry/net/Net.java
index 1b2ef9c95361afdc0ebdb3752a8db9ae3fe1dbb2..3010f166dfa3fd92e52c8c8eb467e09f2abf4e78 100644
--- a/core/src/mindustry/net/Net.java
+++ b/core/src/mindustry/net/Net.java
@@ -298,6 +298,11 @@ public class Net{
             return;
         }
 
+        //MDTX: unit spawn packets are added during handled(); ignore them while the world isn't loaded yet
+        if(object instanceof UnitSpawnCallPacket && world.height() == 0){
+            return;
+        }
+
         try{
             object.handled();
         }catch(RuntimeException e){
